ons  in the middle of that absurdity and i  didn't mention it before but damon  tossing the egg back to renera before he  backed down on the bridge was weirdly  endearing there was a lot of interesting  connections to the original series and i  think my favorite was seeing the sep  that's in king's landing at this time  you'll notice that it's not that sept  the great septa bailor that cersei did  her thing to in the season six finale  that was constructed by and named after  king balor the blessed whose reign  doesn't happen until decades after what  we're watching now having said all of  that i think the side of me that's a fan  of great tv is a little less convinced  this week there were a couple of things  that felt sort of clunky in this episode  and i'll just mention too the sequence  when renera is going to his chambers  after being called to meet with her  father it all felt a little bit off the  score kicks in and it seems like they  wanted to have this build up that didn't  really land there's also this long shot  where you can almost mistake millie  alcock for emilia clarke which i don't  think does either character very many  favors also the long slow reveal that  corliss is talking to damon felt  unnecessary they're just small cracks  but they're the kinds of things that  could add up generally speaking my  enjoyment of the lore allows me to gloss  over these types of things but i hope  this is more about the fact that this is  the first season rather than signs of  not being able to live up to the hype  they have the advantage of mostly  keeping things close to king's landing  with regular trips to dragonstone and  the nerd in me can't wait to see more of  the house valerian seat at driftmark you  do get a nice little tease of some of  the treasures he's collected on his  voyages but this is also a big  undertaking even scaled down westeros is  daunting so i hope they'll be able to  make it all work i would say so far they  are especially in moments like the shot  of the bridge at dragonstone this looked  amazing and they did a good job of  presenting the different sides and what  the motivations were in a way that is  very game of thrones the acting is also  strong there are a ton of great small  moments delivered by everyone and it's  all very promising for what's to come  i'm excited to see what happens next and  i think that's a great place to leave  things let me know in the comments what  you thought about the episode how do you  feel about damon becoming the rogue  prince and i'm especially interested to  see how things landed for people who  don't know what's coming please like  this video if you enjoyed it please  subscribe to my channel if you haven't  already and thanks for watching i'll  talk to you soon

