lt  and the child he's about to marry try to  have a conversation rhaenys and renera  talk and the queen who never was lays  out the reality of the situation even if  it's not to her daughter the king will  remarry and he will produce more heirs  and if one of them is a male then at  least some people will expect him to be  the next king rhaenyra points out that a  lot of lords bent the knee to her and  swore fealty but she's speaking from the  experience of being passed over and says  that the men of the kingdom would rather  put the realm to the torch than let a  woman ascend to the iron throne in some  ways their two situations are quite  different but seeing how the people  closest to the king aren't exactly  jumping in line behind renera does make  it seem like that she's probably not  wrong speaking of being passed over  after not getting his brother's  attention by sitting in dragonstone for  half a year damon decides to steal a  dragon's egg to further stir things up  he says that mazaria is with child that  he'll be making her his second wife like  their ancestors used to do and he  invites his brother to attend the  wedding becerras sees this for what it  is and is almost set to ignore him again  until renera finds out that he took the  same egg she chose to put in bail on the  air for a day's cradle before her mother  died when he hears that he's ready to go  get it back himself but otto steps in  partly because it's his job to keep the  king safe but also because he hates  damon and wants to make it seem like his  brother doesn't care enough about him to  actually go it all makes for a nice shot  of dragonstone where things get pretty  tense everyone present knows this is  going to turn into a bloodbath  especially when caraxes makes an  appearance but it's still a little hard  to see how damon can back down the whole  thing is a farce to get his brother's  attention and it's not working and it  really could have gone sideways if  rhaenyra didn't show up and talk sense  into him i suppose it's obvious but i  still have to mention that this is what  happens when people in these positions  don't get what they want they throw  their little tantrums and other people  end up getting hurt and i thought they  did a pretty good job of showing  mazaria's point of view in this in that  she doesn't appreciate being used as a  prop he thinks that he would be able to  protect her and tries to tell her not to  worry but from her perspective and she's  definitely not wrong she is expendable  and this doesn't do anything but paint a  target on her back she says you are  targaryen you can afford to play your  stupid games with the king which of  course we see that playing out in front  of us in real time she points out that  she isn't there because she wants his  gold or power for herself she came to  him to be liberated from the fear that  she's known for as long as she can  remember this is something that damon  would never consider because the  characters at the center of this story  believe their owed respect and deference  and to get what they want based on who  they are they were born into this and  have had that reinforced throughout  their lives having been raised at the  center of an empire at its height they  like to talk a lot about the duty that  goes along with that but generally still  behave like privileged spoiled brats  because they can generally speaking when  things go wrong because of the decisions  they make they won't experience the  worst of it and so it makes sense here  to show the perspective of someone else  who would back in king's landing  becerras isn't coming around to the idea  of marrying laina and he goes to his  master of laws lionel strong for an  unencumbered opinion he re-tells him all  the reasons why it makes sense in a very  straightforward way with the added she  will mature when faced with the obvious  problem of her being 12. in no uncertain  terms he says you should wed lana  valerian mike grace he should give  corliss what he wants and fix him at his  side permanently before he can respond  he's surprised when he gets word that  the princess has returned from  dragonstone he goes to ream her out  because she's his only heir and she went  behind his back put herself in danger  and if something were to happen then  that would put the future of their house  in question she points out that she did  it to retrieve the egg without bloodshed  she's probably not wrong about not  knowing nevada would have been able to  do that as much as the king is bothered  by what damon's doing he's still his  brother she knows they care about each  other and then he comes around when he  realizes she's a lot like her mother  they share a moment where he again tells  her how hard losing emma has been and  when she tells him that it pleases her  to know that she's not alone in that he  transitions to saying that the small  council is pressuring him to marry it's  a return to the uncomfortable where they  talk about each other in this detached  way as if they're not right there  sitting in front of each other the  actors do a great job of navigating away  from a loving father talking to his  daughter to a king who is bound by duty  in her response renera matches that and  gives him a way out he has to do this  because it's his responsibility as the  king his first duty is to the realm and  she adds that her mother would have  understood just as she does because  these are two people who are not capable  of talking in a completely honest way in  this circumstance you have to look past  the actual words they're saying her  father is telling her that he'll never  replace her mother just like he'd never  replace her as heir but also saying that  they need to do everything they can to  protect their family's position this is  him confirming the first part of what  rhaenys told her earlier she plays the  role she's been given to be supportive  in a selfless way but it's also not  clear if she's pulling it off she didn't  ask to be named air but now that she has  been you can see through her reaction  that she doesn't like the idea of it  being taken away from her he's also  completely talking around what his real  issue with taking a queen is and so when  the small council meets a little later  she's just as caught off guard as  corliss valerian is when he announces  that he's going to marry alison it's a  moment where reality shatters your ideas  about who you are and what you're  capable of ronira had been supportive  she understood the situation and she was  willing to go along with it for her  family faced with the idea of her father  marrying her close friend and being  completely blindsided by it hurts her in  a way that makes her leave the room  corliss reacts exactly as lionel said he  would and leaves himself but unlike  renera we get a chance to see where he  goes with it he invites damon over to  his island to meet with him because as  he presents it they're both men who've  had to cut their way through the world  and you can see where he's coming from  at this point in history his family is  richer than the lannisters or the  hightowers what he's saying about his  personal history is true he built that  up in a way that the likes of the  current targaryens can't understand and  i don't want to go into that completely  right here but he set out on nine great  voyages and made a name for himself  while amassing a fortune his house goes  back to old deliria they might even be  older than the targaryens and i love how  he adds according to some text there but  there's still a big difference since his  family weren't dragon lords by marrying  rhaenys he brought dragons into his  house but forming an alliance with damon  here would allow him to do what he wants  without too much worry about how viserys  might respond they've drilled his  reluctance to move against his brother  into our heads and corliss picked up on  that and it's something he can use to  his advantage plus what he's saying to  win him over here is basically sincere  he knows damon doesn't really have a  place he's got that second sun energy  and now he's outside of the line of  succession the realms fighters are also  itching for action and as the episode  comes to an end you get the sense that  these two might be able to make that  happen as a person who is a big fan of  the world george rr martin created i  can't help but enjoy the chance to dig  back into all of this stuff that part of  me is really enjoying how they're adding  to the story and leaning into presenting  these characters with chances to do  something different there is an  inevitability baked in because most  people know the realm isn't this way  during game of thrones so they are  making the effort to try to make us care  about what happens to these characters i  thought it worked best this week with  alison who spent most of her time pushed  off to the side of everything else that  was going on i liked how they show her  always putting on her best face and  saying the right things while showing  her nervously picking at her fingernails  when she's alone the fact that her  father brings this up in the way he does  and just how clueless that makes him  seem about what she's going through what  he's encouraging her to put herself  through does a lot to add to that  character in the book all of this just  sort of happens off page and that makes  her less sympathetic i think here we see  someone who is doing what she thinks she  has to based on her position and the  world she lives in if you think about it  she gave both father and daughter sound  advice when they confided in her i also  liked that there were some genuinely  funny parts mixed in there viserys just  casually dipping his hand into those  maggots and effortlessly conversing with  otto after seeing him struggle to talk  with his daughter was great little laina  being so pumped up to talk about dragons  in the middle of that absurdity and i  didn't mention it before but damon  tossing the egg back to renera before he  backed down on the bridge was weirdly  endearing there was a lot of interesting  connections to the original series and i  think my favorite was seeing the sep  that's in king's landing at this time  you'll notice that it's not that sept  the great septa bailor that cersei did  her thing to in the season six finale  that was constructed by and named after  king balor the blessed whose reign  doesn't happen until decades after what  we're watching now having said all of  that i think the side of me that's a fan  of great tv is a little less convinced  this week there were a couple of things  that felt sort of clunky in this episode  and i'll just mention too the sequence  when renera is going to his chambers  after being called to meet with her  father it all felt a little bit off the  score kicks in and it seems like they  wanted to have this build up that didn't  really land there's also this long shot  where you can almost mistake millie  alcock for emilia clarke which i don't  think does either character very many  favors also the long slow reveal that  corliss is talking to damon felt  unnecessary they're just small cracks  but they're the kinds of things that  could add up generally speaking my  enjoyment of the lore allows me to gloss  over these types of things but i hope  this is more about the fact that this is  the first season rather than signs of  not being able to live up to the hype  they have the advantage of mostly  keeping things close to king's landing  with regular trips to dragonstone and  the nerd in me can't wait to see more of  the house valerian seat at driftmark you  do get a nice little tease of some of  the treasures he's collected on his  voyages but this is also a big  undertaking even scaled down westeros is  daunting so i hope they'll be able to  make it all work i would say so far they  are especially in moments like the shot  of the bridge at dragonstone this looked  amazing and they did a good job of  presenting the different sides and what  the motivations were in a way that is  very game of thrones the acting is also  strong there are a ton of great small  moments delivered by everyone and it's  all very promising for what's to come  i'm excited to see what happens next and  i think that's a great place to leave  things let me know in the comments what  you thought about the episode how do you  feel about damon becoming the rogue  prince and i'm especially interested to  see how things landed for people who  don't know what's coming please like  this video if you enjoyed it please  subscribe to my channel if you haven't  already and thanks for watching i'll  talk to you soon
 

